ssion prompts for the session, so Claude can cook without being blocked on me.\n\nhttps://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/tree/main/plugins/ralph-wiggum\n\nhttps://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide","raw_text":{"text":"12/ For very long-running tasks, I will either (a) prompt Claude to verify its work with a background agent when it's done, (b) use an agent Stop hook to do that more deterministically, or (c) use the ralph-wiggum plugin (originally dreamt up by @GeoffreyHuntley). I will also use either --permission-mode=dontAsk or --dangerously-skip-permissions in a sandbox to avoid permission prompts for the session, so Claude can cook without being blocked on me.\n\nhttps://t.co/floA4sI7FR\n\nhttps://t.co/klOPZPPgIU","display_text_range":[0,503],"facets":[{"type":"mention","indices":[246,262],"original":"GeoffreyHuntley","id":"14961859"},{"type":"media","indices":[281,304],"id":"2007172638863724544","display":"pic.x.com/o87PZZeWxi","original":"https://t.co/o87PZZeWxi","replacement":"https://x.com/bcherny/status/2007179858435281082/photo/1"},{"type":"url","indices":[455,478],"original":"https://t.co/floA4sI7FR","replacement":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/tree/main/plugins/ralph-wiggum","display":"github.com/anthropics/cla…"},{"type":"url","indices":[480,503],"original":"https://t.co/klOPZPPgIU","replacement":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide","display":"code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-…"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"bcherny","url":"https://x.com/bcherny","id":"159337660","followers":635694,"following":135,"likes":4385,"media_count":124,"statuses":2600,"name":"Boris Cherny","description":"Claude @anthropicai","raw_description":{"text":"Claude @anthropicai","facets":[]},"location":"San Francisco","banner_url":"","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1902044548936953856/J2jeik0t_200x200.jpg","joined":"Fri Jun 25 03:08:49 +0000 2010","protected":false,"website":{"url":"https://borischerny.com","display_url":"borischerny.com"},"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"type":"profile"},"replies":36,"reposts":44,"likes":1243,"bookmarks":789,"quotes":15,"embed_card":"summary_large_image","created_at":"Fri Jan 02 19:59:04 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1767383944,"possibly_sensitive":false,"views":436611,"is_note_tweet":true,"community_note":null,"lang":"en","replying_to":{"screen_name":"bcherny","status":"2007179856266789204","url":"https://x.com/bcherny/status/2007179856266789204","profile_url":"https://x.com/bcherny"},"media":{"all":[{"type":"photo","id":"2007172638863724544","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/G9ro4W5bEAAQ3ug.jpg?name=orig","width":1064,"height":234}],"photos":[{"type":"photo","id":"2007172638863724544","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/G9ro4W5bEAAQ3ug.jpg?name=orig","width":1064,"height":234}]},"provider":"twitter","reposted_by":null},{"type":"status","url":"https://x.com/bcherny/status/2007179861115511237","id":"2007179861115511237","text":"13/ A final tip: probably the most important thing to get great results out of Claude Code -- give Claude a way to verify its work. If Claude has that feedback loop, it will 2-3x the quality of the final result.\n\nClaude tests every single change I land to http://claude.ai/code using the Claude Chrome extension. It opens a browser, tests the UI, and iterates until the code works and the UX feels good.\n\nVerification looks different for each domain. It might be as simple as running a bash command, or running a test suite, or testing the app in a browser or phone simulator. Make sure to invest in making this rock-solid.\n\nhttps://code.claude.com/docs/en/chrome","raw_text":{"text":"13/ A final tip: probably the most important thing to get great results out of Claude Code -- give Claude a way to verify its work. If Claude has that feedback loop, it will 2-3x the quality of the final result.\n\nClaude tests every single change I land to https://t.co/pEWPQoSq5t using the Claude Chrome ex